  "interpretation": [
    "MPPI already consumes aggregate mass/COM/inertia; it does not roll out ten individual arm pendulums.",
    "The remaining per-link CPU transforms and repeated invariant preparation did cost time; state readback alone was about1.7ms.",
    "Two anchors reduce positive-mass payload links from17 to9 and introduce pose-dependent approximation error.",
    "Full-link vector aggregation matches the original scalar arithmetic to floating-point precision. Recorded poses, feet, contacts and applied torques were exactly equal at all600 samples in both matched baseline/candidate runs.",
    "Installed payload means decreased by38..41%; walking-loop means decreased by6.3% for fixed arm and1.0% for moving arm in these single trials. Other stage timing variability, including slower solver and torque stages in the moving run, absorbed some of the saving.",
    "Against optimized full-link aggregation, the two-anchor candidate saved only.009ms fixed/.180ms moving in payload means; it was not consistently faster overall.",
    "The production model remains precise. The10ms real-time step budget is still exceeded during walking; GC and other state/control/readback costs were not changed.",
    "DDS/WebRTC peer sessions and WAN media performance were outside these payload trials."
  ],
